-- phenylalanine, the first compound with a ring. Atoms: 0 carboxyl carbon, 1 and 2 its oxygens, 3 the
-- alpha carbon, 4 its hydrogen, 5 the nitrogen, 6 the beta carbon, 7 and 8 its hydrogens, 9 the ring
-- carbon it attaches to, then the ring: 10 and 12 the two carbons next to it with hydrogens 11 and 13,
-- 14 and 16 the next pair with hydrogens 15 and 17, and 18 the far carbon with hydrogen 19. The ring has
-- a two-fold rotation about the axis through 9 and 18, which is a proper operation and therefore a
-- symmetry under both readings: it identifies the two near ring hydrogens with each other and the two
-- far ones with each other, and that identification is not in dispute between the carriers.
num-phe-obs : List Nat
num-phe-obs = cons 4 (cons 7 (cons 8 (cons 11 (cons 13 (cons 15 (cons 17 (cons 19 nil)))))))
